{"activity_text": "Antifungal, candidacidal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of THE PEPTIDE shows 40.9% similarity to Lividin 8 HLmb. Activity: Active against S. aureus ATCC29213M (MIC>120 uM), S. epidermidis ATCC12228 (MIC>120 uM), M.luteus BR2 (MIC >120 uM), M. luteus A270 (MIC 60-120 uM), Gram- P. aeruginosa ATCC27853 (MIC 60-120 uM), E.coli D31 or SBS363 (MIC > 120 uM), S. marcescens ATCC4112 (MIC 60-120 uM), E.cloacae beta12 (MIC > 120 uM), fungi C. albicans MDM8 or IOC4558 (MIC 7.5-30 uM), C. guilliermondii (MIC 3.8-7.5 uM) and C. tropicalis (MIC 3.8-7.5 uM), filamentous fungi A.niger (MIC> 120 uM), C.herbarum ATCC26362 (MIC> 120 uM), and P.farinosus IBCB251 (MIC> 120 uM). Also, longipin can form amyloid-like structure (Amyloid AMPs). Updated 12/2024", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "27997568", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2016 Dec 20;11(12):e0167953. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02764", "source_id": "AP02764", "source_numeric_id": "02764", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02764", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Longipin: An Amyloid Antimicrobial Peptide from the Harvestman Acutisoma longipes (Arachnida: Opiliones) with Preferential Affinity for Anionic Vesicles", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
